`cargo fmt --all` is clean and `cargo check -q --all-targets` covers all four touched crates. The panic-site ratchet
moved by exactly two tokens, in `xai-grok-test-support` (26 -> 28 `panic!`), and those two are the mechanism: the
deliberate `panic!("a holder dying inside the guard")` inside the two new poisoning helpers. `unwrap_or_else(
PoisonError::into_inner)` counts as nothing, which is why the helpers, and everything in this batch, spell
recovery that way rather than as `.unwrap()`.

== 9. Remote CI could not be used as the reviewer of record

This batch and the one before it would normally be signed off by the `CI` workflow. From this host that endpoint
cannot be trusted, and the proof is not a timeout but ten readings of one run that cannot all be true. Run
`37304357103`, workflow `CI`, `head_sha` `1da04e67`, started `2026-10-05T11:39:42Z`; the only non-instant job is
`rust check / clippy / test`, id `111744342738`. All readings taken inside about 30 minutes with the same token.

| # | Source | Reading |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `gh run list --commit 1da04e67` | run `37282718918` `completed cancelled` (that id 404s and is absent from the last 100 runs) |
| 2 | `gh api .../runs/37304357103` | `status=completed` with `conclusion=in_progress` |
| 3 | `gh api .../runs/37304357103/jobs` | 8 jobs, all `completed`, all `success` |
| 4 | same URL two minutes later | 7 jobs, `rust check / clippy / test` `in_progress` |
| 5 | `/commits/1da04e67/check-runs` | 8 check runs, rust `in_progress`, 7 `success` |
| 6 | `/actions/runs/37304357103/jobs`, 3 reads 5 s apart | job `111744342738` `in_progress`, first 12 steps `success` |
| 7 | watcher on check-runs, 2 reads 90 s apart | rust job `completed` + `failure` |
| 8 | `-L /actions/jobs/111744342738/logs` | HTTP 404 `BlobNotFound` (Azure timestamp `12:03:17Z`) |
| 9 | same URL 13 s later | HTTP 200, body contained `all gates passed` |
| 10 | the same file, read back immediately | 2 lines, `BlobNotFound`, Azure timestamp `12:03:30Z` |

Readings 9 and 10 are the decisive pair: a finalized log blob does not revert to `BlobNotFound`, so the 200 in 9 was
not a real GitHub response. Reading 8 also dates the job -- at `12:03Z` the log for a job that started at `11:39Z`
does not exist yet, i.e. it was about 24 minutes into a run that needs about 40.

What this batch therefore does: readings 3 and 7 are discarded and reported nowhere as a CI result; no monitor is
armed on any Actions endpoint; the gate evidence of record is the host sweep plus the named local runs above, all of
them reproducible without a network. **The CI verdict for `1da04e67` is unknown from this machine, and this batch's
pushed commit should be read the same way until someone opens the run in a browser.** A durable row records it.

== 10. Reproduce it

    python3 scripts/ci/test-check-lock-poison.py            # the gate's fixtures
    python3 scripts/ci/check-lock-poison.py --root . --verbose
    python3 scripts/ci/check-lock-poison.py --inventory     # the shapes the gate allows, counted
    python3 scripts/ci/check-guard-wiring.py                # both runners reach the gate
    cargo test -q -p xai-grok-telemetry --lib client::      # both poisoning tests, both modes
    cargo test -q -p xai-grok-sampler --lib doom_loop
    RUST_MIN_STACK=16777216 cargo test -q -p xai-grok-pager --lib git_info::
    RUST_MIN_STACK=16777216 cargo test -q -p xai-grok-shell --lib cached_remote_survives_a_poisoned_lock

To re-run the matrix, splice `git show HEAD:<file>`'s text back over the converted site and run the one test named
for it in section 7, restoring from a byte copy and comparing hashes afterwards. The driver that automates that --
including the baseline guard and the 13 cell descriptions -- lives outside the repository; the cell list it enforces
is section 7's table.
